## PART 2 — WHAT IS MISSING (Build next, in priority order)

### Priority 1 — Visual & UX improvements (adopt from spec, build in existing codebase)

#### 1a. Landing page hero animation (SVG moving vehicles)
**Why:** The spec describes a "living mobility interface" — vehicles moving on an animated map. 
**Currently:** Static hero with framer-motion fade-in only.
**Build:** Add `components/landing/HeroAnimation.tsx` — pure SVG + CSS animateMotion.
- 6 vehicle markers moving along pre-drawn routes
- Cyan/blue color scheme matching brand
- Geofence pulse rings
- Radar ping dots
- prefers-reduced-motion: static fallback
- IntersectionObserver: pause when scrolled away
- No JS animation loop — SVG SMIL runs on compositor thread

#### 1b. Nav scroll behavior
**Currently:** Nav is always white/styled.
**Build:** At scroll position 0 → transparent on hero. After 40px → blur backdrop navy.
Transition: 300ms. Already have the CSS class pattern in spec.

#### 1c. Login page vehicle-door animation
**Currently:** Clean dark card, good quality.
**Adopt from spec (partial):** Keep the existing form exactly. Add a subtle animated element — a vehicle silhouette SVG on the right half of the desktop layout. On mobile, keep current centered card. This adds brand identity without breaking the working auth flow.

#### 1d. Feature-gated sidebar items with lock icons
**Currently:** Items are hidden if not accessible.
**Spec says:** Show them with 🔒 or ⛔ icon, let them click and see an explanatory message.
**Build:** Update `Sidebar.tsx` — grayed items instead of hidden ones + Message A/B pages.

#### 1e. Dark map tiles (currently uses OpenStreetMap default light)
**Adopt from spec:** Switch to CartoDB Dark Matter tiles in authenticated map.
`https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/dark_all/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png`
Matches the navy brand palette. One-line change in LiveMap.tsx.

#### 1f. Tailwind color token extension
**Currently:** Uses `brand-` prefix with some inline hex.
**Build:** Add navy-950 through navy-500, cyan, teal, auditor/delegate/impersonate to tailwind.config.ts.
This is a non-breaking config change only.

