### Priority 3 — Backend additions needed

#### 3a. Personal user role system
**Currently:** Every user must have organizationId (required in schema).
**Problem:** Personal accounts (owner/driver/customer) get a throwaway "personal org" — workable but not clean.
**Fix (Phase 2):** Make organizationId nullable, add PersonalRole model, context-based API scoping.
**For now:** The "personal org" approach works. Document it and live with it until Phase 2.

#### 3b. Context-scoped API middleware
**Currently:** API routes check `req.user.organizationId` for scoping.
**Spec says:** Add `X-Context-Type` + `X-Context-Id` headers for multi-role users.
**Build:** Middleware that reads the context header, validates the grant, and attaches `req.context` with scoped permissions. Existing routes continue to work (backward compatible — fallback to organizationId if no context header).

#### 3c. Trip/dispatch model
**Currently:** Trip table exists in schema but no routes.
**Build:** `POST /trips`, `GET /trips`, `PATCH /trips/:id/assign`, `PATCH /trips/:id/status`.

#### 3d. Owner portal backend
**Build:** `GET /owner/vehicles` (filter by ownerUserId), `GET /owner/statements`, `GET /owner/payouts`.
Requires adding `ownerUserId` field to Vehicle schema + migration.

#### 3e. Feature entitlement system
**Currently:** No feature-gating — all features available to all companies.
**Build (Phase 2):** `feature_catalog`, `plan_features`, `company_entitlements` tables.
For now: skip feature gating on backend, but build the `FeatureGate` component on frontend as a no-op wrapper (always passes). This way the UI is ready when backend catches up.

#### 3f. Cloud/S3 file storage
**Currently:** Documents stored in `/uploads` on server filesystem.
**Risk:** Data loss if container restarts without a volume mount.
**Check:** Verify docker-compose.yml has a named volume for uploads.
**Fix:** Add `./uploads:/app/uploads` volume mount in docker-compose (quick fix). 
**Phase 2:** Migrate to S3/R2 with signed URLs.

#### 3g. Prisma migrations for new features
When adding owner portal, trips, context system — each needs a migration.
Always test locally: `npx prisma migrate dev --name <name>` before pushing.

---

### Priority 4 — Architecture improvements (spec best practices to adopt)

#### 4a. Socket.IO context scoping
**Currently:** All users in an org see all their org's vehicle updates.
**Spec says:** Scope subscriptions by context (customer sees only booking vehicle, driver sees only their vehicle).
**Build:** In the Socket.IO connection handler, validate the user's context and only join rooms for vehicles they're authorized to see.

#### 4b. Vehicle status freshness indicators
**Currently:** Markers change color by status (ACTIVE/IDLE/OFFLINE) but no "last seen X seconds ago" shown.
**Adopt from spec:** Add `ageSeconds` and `accuracyM` to Socket.IO `location:update` payload.
Show "last seen 3s ago · ±8m" in vehicle popup and vehicle list.

#### 4c. Map marker visual improvements
**Currently:** Custom Leaflet divIcon markers exist.
**Adopt from spec:** Add CSS pulse animation on ACTIVE markers, dim + no pulse on OFFLINE, status color transitions (240ms ease).
**Build:** Update `marker.css` or inline styles in `LiveMap.tsx`.

#### 4d. Tabular numbers for data
**Currently:** Plain text for speeds, amounts, distances.
**Adopt:** Add `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-family: monospace` to all numeric cells in tables.
One CSS class `.tabular` applied to cells. Prevents column width jitter on live updates.

#### 4e. Page transition animations
**Currently:** No page transition.
**Adopt:** Framer-motion `AnimatePresence` on page content only (not sidebar/topbar).
Outgoing: opacity 0, 100ms. Incoming: opacity 0→1 + translateY(8px)→0, 200ms.
Low-risk improvement — framer-motion is already installed.

#### 4f. Reduced-motion compliance
**Currently:** framer-motion respects this by default via `useReducedMotion()`.
**Audit:** Check all CSS keyframe animations (loading spinner, etc.) have `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` overrides.

