## PART 10 — THE SINGLE MOST IMPORTANT IMPROVEMENT

From all the spec documents, one principle stands out as the highest-leverage change for the current codebase:

> **Show locked features — don't hide them.**

Currently: if a user can't access a page, it disappears from the sidebar.
Spec says: keep it visible but grayed, let them click, show who to contact.

This single change:
- Makes users aware of features their org could unlock (drives upgrade requests)
- Reduces "why is X missing?" support tickets  
- Makes the product feel complete rather than bare
- Takes about 2 hours to implement (Sidebar.tsx + 2 message pages)

Build this in Phase A before anything else.

